{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821116-conquering-heroes","id":821116,"title":"Conquering Heroes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-01T12:02:21-08:00","id":821116,"title":"Conquering Heroes","content":"Is there anything in particular anyone is hoping for in Beast's upcoming Night Horrors book? Personally I'd like to see an example or two of less homicidal Heroes that can still serve as antagonists to the Children of the Dark Mother.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T13:00:39-08:00","id":821149,"title":"","content":"Running Heroes in other games or, &quot;shut up, Steve, we aren't taking on a Dragon right now.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T15:01:30-08:00","id":821229,"title":"","content":"Hopefully there's a corresponding threat in the Primordial Dream that can menace Horrors directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:04:15-08:00","id":821307,"title":"","content":"More stuff from the Temenos that's ideologically in conflict with Fear. The rise and fall of these Goetia's prominence could influence the Primordial Dream. For example, when more people speak of hope and engage in hopeful activities, the more Beasts find their powers and Hungers reacting strangely.<br /> <br /> Ancient Heroes who have come to the modern world in one way or another and are not amused by the new meaning of Heroism.<br /> <br /> Lesser critters from the Primordial Dream that are not Horrors and can invade the waking world through certain dreams. They could be impish little bastards, or a sort of Familiar after investment and risk-taking. Every Family needs a pet, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T17:49:15-08:00","id":821335,"title":"","content":"I remember Secrets of the Ruined Temple mentioning Chimerical Beasts- essentially the Begotten long before the Begotten were even a thing -as some Temenos strangeness Mages may have to deal with. They were mythical creatures made flesh, creatures consumed by their hungers.<br /> <br /> They also mentioned a second kind of enfleshed Goetics- Eidolons, ancient gods and heroes reborn. If that's not something to look into, I don't know what is.<br /> <br /> That being said, I find the idea of Ancient Heroes somehow emerging from the Dream and wanting to slap their successors upside the head rather entertaining. What Heroes were originally supposed to be, people who faced the Horrors in the dark and took lessons from the conflict back to the people, sounds really quite awe-inspiring, genuinely heroic in my books. I'm already picturing how these guys would interact with Neolithic Wise as detailed in The Sundered World. I wonder where it all went wrong?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":4152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","user":"Arcanist","date":". 02-01-2016, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T18:00:05-08:00","id":821338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821116-conquering-heroes?p=821307#post821307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More stuff from the Temenos that's ideologically in conflict with Fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Primordial Dream being home to a bunch of legendary nightmares doesn't make it &quot;the Temenos realm of Fear&quot; and to treat it as such is reductive in the extreme.<br /> <br /> Utopias are a dime a dozen in the Bright Dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T18:26:47-08:00","id":821350,"title":"","content":"Satchel, what eldritch lore are you possessed of that you can so accurately and succinctly describe the lore and cosmology of the CofD? It is unfailingly accurate and extremely impressive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T19:28:19-08:00","id":821378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-ic