CofD? It is unfailingly accurate and extremely impressive.</div> </div> </div> </div> They're an Analyst Exile with a focus on the fictional metastructures we call &quot;RPGs&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:38:39-08:00","id":821410,"title":"","content":"Now I'm wondering what an Eidolon would be like as a playable splat. Obviously they'd share traits with Heroes but would they have Atavism and Nightmare - like powers? Would they have something similar to Hungers? Would they have a dream realm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T20:43:14-08:00","id":821414,"title":"","content":"A werewolf pack that focuses on hunting Beasts. A member of the Ordo Dracul who believes vampires can transcend to Beasthood, leaving the flaws of vampirism behind. A few individuals that don't fit the known templates, either monsters or more humanoid threats. Some sort of Astral dream beast that claims to be a herald of the Dark Mother. Some more common supernatural that has been screwed over by Beasts and is out for revenge. A mage Hero.<br /> <br /> And a Hero who is also a high ranking politician, preferably without poking at a specific real life politician.<br /> <br /> A Hero with a magic sword, one magical before the Weaponbound Anathema was used. A Beast who is trying and perhaps succeeding to a point in organizing fellow Beasts, but killing those opposed to about the idea. An 'Infernal' Beast, like proposed in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/820371-portraying-beast-as-inferno\">this thread.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-02-2016, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:07:28-08:00","id":821424,"title":"","content":"Could a Mage still be a Hero? I know that Mages generally keep (or convert into Arcane XP) any supernatural Merits or gifts they possess from Minor Templates. You can have Demon Blooded and Wolf Blooded Mages, but I'm not sure if Heroes are close enough to baseline human.<br /> <br /> That being said, a Hero who hasn't hit the &quot;compelled to hunt&quot; threshold would be inclined towards an Awakening since they naturally dream their way pretty deep into the Astral Realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:17:12-08:00","id":821426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821116-conquering-heroes?p=821424#post821424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could a Mage still be a Hero? I know that Mages generally keep (or convert into Arcane XP) any supernatural Merits or gifts they possess from Minor Templates. You can have Demon Blooded and Wolf Blooded Mages, but I'm not sure if Heroes are close enough to baseline human.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of my favorite characters in the Night Horrors line is Billy Vines, a vampire who can freely walk around in the sun. The books are toolboxes, and the Chronicles of Darkness are not limited by those toolboxes and what's inside them. Part of the fun is when what is expected is turned on its head, or side, rather than being a reiteration of the Beasts and Heroes available in the core.<br /> <br /> I don't believe Mages can traditionally become Heroes as, among other things, Heroes have Integrity and not Wisdom. Though Banishers do seem to be working off of Integrity.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:24:41-08:00","id":821428,"title":"","content":"Doesn't stop a Mage being a Hero pre-Awakening though. Mages still use Virtue and Vice, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-01T21:26:25-08:00","id":821429,"title":"","content":"At least one semicredible manifestation of the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> Examples of Beasts who've naturalized themselves into the metaphysics of other parts of the cosmology, particularly the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Examples of weird and/or esoteric Lair Traits and the Beasts who developed them.<br /> <br /> A demon missing one or more of the usual deficiencies that stymie interaction with the Begotten.<br /> <br /> Kinships with objects, places, or phenomena.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"",