icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't stop a Mage being a Hero pre-Awakening though. Mages still use Virtue and Vice, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, but a merit reward for being an ex-Hero could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:06:48-08:00","id":821738,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexmeister Vic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821116-conquering-heroes?p=821683#post821683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, but a merit reward for being an ex-Hero could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe a Mind and/or Fate Legacy that focuses on making other people conform to a narrative?<br /> <br /> Anyway, it might be interesting to see some sort or &quot;Nightmare Shamans&quot;, normal humans who have learned to channel the Primordial Dream, and who can ally with or harvest the Begotten for more power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T13:41:45-08:00","id":821856,"title":"","content":"More on 'Hercules' Heroes (I think this got cut from 2nd draft but I still like the conceit) who have slain dozens of begotten and live for centuries. Something that can challenge an Incarnate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T14:12:15-08:00","id":821870,"title":"","content":"Incarnates being the &quot;legendary monster, uncontested master of their own story&quot; endgame, explicitely untouchable by the ego-driven tales of Heroes, I don't think we're ever going to see an example of the latter being able to straight up challenge an Incarnate.<br /> <br /> Exceptions are a rule in the Chronicles Of Darkness of course, but I don't feel this would be a particularly flattering one to the concept. That and if a Hero, themselves legendary or not, wants to bring down an Incarnate, they should strike at the foundation of power that is the Beast's Myth.<br /> <br /> I do hope we'll see some impressive Heroes with unique gifts, as well as more diversity in their nature and abilities.<br /> <br /> In the same vein, Incarnates whose myth has grown in new and unexpected ways, and Begotten or their remnants who have uniquely adapted to one of the other realms in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-02-2016, 05:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T14:49:15-08:00","id":821886,"title":"","content":"Another rough weird idea I've had is bloodlines of mortals who have some sort of minor link to the Primordial Dream (Incarnate heritage or someone only being invested with part of a Horror are both theoretical origins), though I'm nor sure what I'd call them. The idea is that people born to this lineage gets a single Atavism (whether as one for the entire bloodline or if each family is assigned a Family and a member is born with a random one from that category, I'm not sure) whose power is linked to their sanity. Off the top of my head, I'd say they could use Integrity in place of Satiety for all intents or purposes, and probably give them something similar in regards to the &quot;Unstable Soul&quot; system used by the Nephilim from the Demon Storyteller's Guide. This is all off the top of my head, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T17:43:08-08:00","id":822012,"title":"","content":"I'm now chuckling at the idea of a Nephil from the Demon Storyteller's Guide running into one of these Primordial Dream Lineages who happen to be Anakim- 